   285→      - trait-shadow-commit
   286→    title: Shadow Branch Auto-Commit
   287→    type: trait
   288→    description: Commands that modify shadow branch state automatically commit changes with semantic messages
   289→    acceptance_criteria:
   290→      - id: ac-1
   291→        given: command modifies state in shadow worktree
   292→        when: save operation completes successfully
   293→        then: git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message
   294→      - id: ac-2
   295→        given: shadow commit is created
   296→        when: commit message is generated
   297→        then: message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail
   298→      - id: ac-3
   299→        given: shadow commit is created
   300→        when: item reference is available
   301→        then: commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug
   302→      - id: ac-4
   303→        given: shadow is not configured (no worktree)
   304→        when: command that would normally commit runs
   305→        then: command completes successfully without attempting git operations
   306→      - id: ac-5
   307→        given: save operation fails
   308→        when: validation or IO error occurs
   309→        then: no commit is attempted and error is returned
   310→      - id: ac-6
   311→        given: shadow has remote configured
   312→        when: commit succeeds
   313→        then: push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)
   314→      - id: ac-7
   315→        given: commit or push fails
   316→        when: save succeeded but git operation failed
   317→        then: command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state
   318→      - id: ac-8
   319→        given: command performs multiple related saves
   320→        when: all saves complete successfully
   321→        then: single atomic commit covers all changes
