   323→    slugs:
   324→      - trait-websocket-protocol
   325→    title: WebSocket Protocol Patterns
   326→    type: trait
   327→    description: WebSocket connection patterns including lifecycle management, topic-based pub/sub,
   328→      heartbeat ping/pong, sequence tracking for deduplication, and backpressure handling. Based on
   329→      proven patterns from kynetic project.
   330→    acceptance_criteria:
   331→      - id: ac-1
   332→        given: WebSocket connection is established
   333→        when: client connects
   334→        then: server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id
   335→      - id: ac-2
   336→        given: client wants notifications
   337→        when: subscribe command sent with topics array
   338→        then: server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id
   339→      - id: ac-3
   340→        given: client is subscribed to topic
   341→        when: relevant change occurs
   342→        then: server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}
   343→      - id: ac-4
   344→        given: WebSocket connection is active
   345→        when: 30 seconds pass without activity
   346→        then: server sends ping frame
   347→      - id: ac-5
   348→        given: ping was sent
   349→        when: no pong received within 90 seconds
   350→        then: connection is closed with code 1001
   351→      - id: ac-6
   352→        given: server sends events
   353→        when: client cannot keep up (backpressure)
   354→        then: server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event
   355→      - id: ac-7
   356→        given: connection is closing
   357→        when: close initiated
   358→        then: use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error
   359→      - id: ac-8
   360→        given: client reconnects after disconnect
   361→        when: new connection established
   362→        then: client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence
